# Pending-triage CVEs for the database image scan gate.
#
# Entries here are CVEs recorded as `under_investigation` in the OpenVEX
# document (docker/db/vex/simis-cms-db.openvex.json). Trivy's VEX filtering
# only suppresses `not_affected`/`fixed` statements, so pending entries live
# here, each with an expiry (`CVE-XXXX-NNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD`), until triage
# resolves them. When a CVE is triaged: update its VEX statement and remove
# its line here. A lapsed expiry re-fails the publish gate on the next run --
# deliberately, so triage cannot be forgotten silently.
#
# CVE-2026-66046 exp:2026-09-10
#   libexpat1 (Expat DoS, no fixed version published by Debian). Entered 2026-08-27 to
#   unblock the publish gate, which had stopped all delivery.
#
#   Not a new exploitability claim: libexpat1 is already in GDAL_CHAIN in
#   tools/generate-db-vex.py, so the existing, reviewed policy resolves it to
#   not_affected (vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path) on the same basis as the rest of
#   the GDAL stack -- vector PostGIS only, postgis_raster never created, so GDAL's XML
#   readers are never loaded. The VEX document cannot say so yet only because
#   generate-db-vex.py reads open Trivy alerts from code scanning, and this CVE has not
#   been ingested there; the live scan in the publish workflow found it first. This line
#   is the bridge until the alert lands and the document can be regenerated.
#
#   To resolve: once the alert appears in code scanning, regenerate
#   (python3 tools/generate-db-vex.py > docker/db/vex/simis-cms-db.openvex.json),
#   confirm the statement reads not_affected, and delete this entry.
CVE-2026-66046 exp:2026-09-10

